---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { states, services } from '../../data/states.js';
const phone = "(833) 722-3359";
const phoneHref = "tel:+18552887767";
---

<Base
  title="Concrete Services Cost Guide 2026 — TX, FL, CA, AZ, CO | USA Concrete Jobs"
  description="Typical costs for concrete cutting, waterproofing, driveway replacement, foundation repair, stamped concrete, and pool decks across Texas, Florida, California, Arizona, and Colorado."
  canonical="https://usaconcretejobs.com/cost/"
>

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Concrete Services Cost Guide — 2026</h1>
      <p>Typical pricing for concrete cutting, waterproofing, driveway replacement, foundation repair, and decorative concrete across our 5 service states.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-section">

      <h2>Cost by Service Type</h2>
      <p>The following ranges represent typical project costs for each service. Actual costs depend on project scope, site conditions, concrete thickness, rebar presence, and local labor rates.</p>

      <table class="cost-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Service</th><th>Typical Cost Range</th><th>Key Cost Factors</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {services.map(service => (
            <tr>
              <td><a href={`/services/${service.slug}/`}><strong>{service.name}</strong></a></td>
              <td class="cost-highlight">{service.avgCost}</td>
              <td style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--color-text-muted);">{service.keyFacts[0]}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px;">Cost by State</h2>
      <p>Labor costs, permit fees, and material costs vary significantly by state. Here are the typical ranges for core services in each state we serve.</p>

      <table class="cost-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>State</th><th>Concrete Cutting</th><th>Waterproofing</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {states.map(state => (
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{state.name}</strong></td>
              <td class="cost-highlight">{state.avgCuttingCost}</td>
              <td class="cost-highlight">{state.avgWaterproofingCost}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px;">Factors That Affect Concrete Cutting Cost</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Concrete thickness:</strong> 4" residential slab vs. 12"+ commercial foundation significantly affects cutting time and blade wear</li>
        <li><strong>Rebar presence:</strong> Cutting through reinforced concrete requires diamond blades and takes longer</li>
        <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Confined spaces, upper floors, or difficult angles add cost</li>
        <li><strong>Cut length and type:</strong> Wall saw vs. flat saw vs. core drill have different day rates</li>
        <li><strong>Permit requirements:</strong> Structural permits can add $200–$800 to total project cost</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px;">Factors That Affect Waterproofing Cost</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Interior vs. exterior:</strong> Exterior waterproofing requires excavation and costs 2–3× more</li>
        <li><strong>Severity of water intrusion:</strong> Active leaks with hydrostatic pressure cost more to fix</li>
        <li><strong>Square footage:</strong> Larger basements and crawl spaces cost more per project</li>
        <li><strong>Drainage system:</strong> Adding a French drain or sump pump adds $1,500–$4,000</li>
        <li><strong>Climate:</strong> States with higher water tables (FL) or clay soils (TX) often require more robust systems</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:48px;">Factors That Affect Driveway Replacement Cost</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Size:</strong> A standard 2-car driveway (400–600 sq ft) vs. a large estate driveway (2,000+ sq ft)</li>
        <li><strong>Demo & haul-away:</strong> Removing old concrete or asphalt adds $500–$2,000</li>
        <li><strong>Base preparation:</strong> Poor soil may require additional gravel base or compaction</li>
        <li><strong>Finish type:</strong> Standard broom finish vs. stamped or exposed aggregate</li>
        <li><strong>Permits:</strong> Required in most municipalities when connecting to a public street</li>
      </ul>

      <div style="margin-top: 40px; text-align:center;">
        <p style="font-size:1.1rem; margin-bottom:16px;">Get an accurate quote for your project — free, no obligation.</p>
        <a href={phoneHref} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">📞 Call {phone} — Free Estimate</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 16px; color:var(--color-text-muted);">or</span>
        <a href="/jobs/post/" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">Post a Job &amp; Get Multiple Bids</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
